{
  "assessment": "The source provides a complete derivation of the flight-size PDF for two regimes: constant pore length and exponentially distributed pore length, both with constant diving rate. These regimes share the same control (flight distance x) and readout (flight-size PDF p(x)), and each yields a quantitative exponential decay law with a characteristic length. The cluster is supported by the supplement lines 370-443. The main-text model (variable diving rate, Gamma-distributed pore lengths) is not selected per the routing hint. The extracted evidence supports a numeric control (x), a numeric readout (p(x)), a quantitative mechanism (exponential decay), and an objective response within an explicit domain, so case_authoring_ready is true.",
